  "summary": "The Coralville, Iowa city council voted 3-2 to adopt guidelines governing use of its newly signed two-year Flock Safety ALPR contract, despite public pleas to cancel the deal. The policy limits searches to law enforcement purposes, bars use solely for immigration, requires case numbers and reasons for queries, and sets a 30-day retention window.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The policy also makes clear that plate reader data cannot be used for any abusive purpose or \"solely for immigration purposes.\"",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "All data is kept for 30 days before it is fully deleted from the Amazon Web Services-owned server where it is stored under the terms of the current contract",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    },
    {
      "quote": "We are not talking about trash removal. We are talking about mass surveillance.",
      "paragraph_idx": 21
    }
  ],
